ind. But in the given facts, Anne's kindness isn't mentioned. So that's a point to note, but it doesn't affect Bob's case.\n\nBack to Bob: He's rough, so white. White, so kind. Rough and kind, so smart. Therefore, Bob is smart, making the statement \"Bob is not smart\" false.\n\nSo the answer should be B) False.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Bob is not smart\" is false because Bob is rough and kind, which according to the rules, makes him smart.\n\n**Answer: B) False**",
