messages:    8%|8         | 50/600 [11:20<1:02:06,  6.78s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is big. Anne is cold. Anne is furry. Anne is white. Erin is cold. Fiona is round. Gary is smart. All smart things are furry. Big, blue things are round. If Gary is cold then Gary is smart. All blue, furry things are big. If Gary is furry then Gary is blue. Round things are cold. Cold, white things are furry. Round things are blue.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Anne is cold.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "Anne is cold" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context.Let me start by listing out all the information provided and then see how it connects.\n\nFirst, let\'s list all the facts:.\n\n1.Anne is big.\n2.Anne is cold.\n3.Anne is furry.\n4.Anne is white.\n5.Erin is cold.\n6.Fiona is round.\n7.Gary is smart.\n8.All smart things are furry.\n9.Big, blue things are round.\n10.If Gary is cold, then Gary is smart.\n11.All blue, furry things are big.\n12.If Gary is furry, then Gary is blue.\n13.Round things are cold.\n14.Cold, white things are furry.\n15.Round things are blue.\n\nWait, but the question is about Anne being cold.From the context, point 2 directly says Anne is cold.So, at first glance, it seems like the answer is True.But maybe I should check if there\'s any conflicting information or if the rules imply something else.\n\nLet me go through each point step by step.\n\nAnne\'s attributes:.\n- Big (1).\n- Cold (2).\n- Furry (3).\n- White (4).\n\nSo, according to the given context, Anne is cold.That\'s straightforward.But perhaps I should verify if the other rules affect this.\n\nLooking at the other rules:.\n\nPoint 14: Cold, white things are furry.Anne is cold, white, and furry, so that fits.So that\'s consistent.\n\nPoint 13: Round things are cold.But Anne is big, not necessarily round.Fiona is round, so Fiona is cold (from 13).Erin is cold (5), so that\'s another cold entity.\n\nPoint 9: Big, blue things are round.So if something is big and blue, it\'s round.But Anne is big and white, so unless she\'s blue, this doesn\'t apply.But Anne is white, so she\'s not blue.Therefore, this rule doesn\'t affect Anne.\n\nPoint 11: All blue, furry things are big.Since Anne is furry and white, not blue, this doesn\'t apply to her.Anne is not cold.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
