ie is smart and blue.From fact 10, all blue, smart things are furry.So Charlie is furry.\n\nWait, but let\'s check if there\'s any contradiction.Let\'s see if being furry affects anything else.From fact 8, furry and nice things are white.Charlie is nice (from fact 12) and furry (from fact 10).So according to fact 8, Charlie should be white.\n\nBut wait, from fact 16, Charlie is nice, so he\'s blue.So he\'s both blue and white?That seems contradictory because something can\'t be both blue and white unless specified otherwise.Let me check the facts again.\n\nWait, fact 8 says "Furry, nice things are white."So if something is both furry and nice, it\'s white.Charlie is both, so he must be white.But from fact 16, being nice makes him blue.So is it possible for something to be both blue and white?The context doesn\'t explicitly say that something can\'t be both, but in reality, objects can have multiple colors.Charlie is not white, according to the given facts.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
