n\n4. From statement 19: If cow needs mouse and mouse sees cow, then mouse is big.\n\n5. From statement 23: If someone is big and sees BE, then they need mouse.\n\n6. From statement 22: If someone is big, they see BE.\n\n7. From statement 4: Cow is big, so cow sees BE (from statement 22).\n\n8. From statement 23: Cow is big and sees BE \u2192 cow needs mouse.\n\n9. Now, cow needs mouse (from step 8) and mouse sees cow (statement 11), so from statement 19, mouse is big.\n\n10. Since mouse is big (from step 9), from statement 22, mouse sees BE.\n\n11. Now, mouse is big (step 9) and sees BE (step 10), so from statement 23, mouse needs mouse.\n\nTherefore, mouse needs mouse, so the statement \"The mouse does not need the mouse\" is false.\n\nSo, the answer is B) False.\n</think>\n\nThe mouse needs itself based on the logical deductions from the given statements. Therefore, the statement \"The mouse does not need the mouse\" is false.\n\n**Answer: B) False**",
