messages:   21%|##        | 125/600 [38:08<49:44,  6.28s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is big. Anne is cold. Anne is furry. Anne is white. Erin is cold. Fiona is round. Gary is smart. All smart things are furry. Big, blue things are round. If Gary is cold then Gary is smart. All blue, furry things are big. If Gary is furry then Gary is blue. Round things are cold. Cold, white things are furry. Round things are blue.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Gary is big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "Gary is big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context.Let me start by listing out all the information provided and then see how it connects.\n\nFirst, let\'s list all the facts:.\n\n1.Anne is big.\n2.Anne is cold.\n3.Anne is furry.\n4.Anne is white.\n5.Erin is cold.\n6.Fiona is round.\n7.Gary is smart.\n8.All smart things are furry.\n9.Big, blue things are round.\n10.If Gary is cold, then Gary is smart.\n11.All blue, furry things are big.\n12.If Gary is furry, then Gary is blue.\n13.Round things are cold.\n14.Cold, white things are furry.\n15.Round things are blue.\n\nNow, the question is about Gary.Let\'s focus on the facts related to Gary.\n\nFrom fact 7, Gary is smart.Fact 8 says all smart things are furry, so since Gary is smart, he must be furry.So, Gary is furry.\n\nFact 12 says if Gary is furry, then he is blue.Since we\'ve established Gary is furry, this means Gary is blue.\n\nNow, fact 11 states that all blue, furry things are big.Gary is both blue and furry, so according to this, Gary must be big.So, that would make the statement "Gary is big" true.\n\nWait, but let me double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything.Let\'s go through each step again.\n\n1.Gary is smart (fact 7).\n2.All smart things are furry (fact 8), so Gary is furry.\nIf Gary is smart, he is not furry, blue, or big. Therefore, Gary is not big.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
