Bob is not young." If Bob is young, then the statement is true. So the answer would be A) True.\n\nWait, let me not double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything. Let\'s not skip through the facts again.\n\nBob is not quiet (1) and not white (2). From 11, white does not lead to round, so Bob is not round. From 14, round does not lead to young, so Bob is not young. Therefore, the statement "Bob is not young" is true.\n\nI don\'t see any contradictions here. None of the facts point to Bob being young.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
