messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nThe bald eagle is big. The bald eagle likes the cow. The bald eagle sees the rabbit. The cow is big. The cow sees the bald eagle. The dog is big. The dog is young. The dog likes the bald eagle. The rabbit sees the bald eagle. The rabbit visits the bald eagle. If the bald eagle sees the rabbit then the rabbit is big. If something likes the bald eagle then it is blue. If something likes the rabbit and the rabbit visits the cow then the cow is young. If something visits the rabbit then it is round. If something is round and it sees the cow then the cow sees the rabbit. If something is big then it visits the cow. If something sees the rabbit then the rabbit visits the bald eagle. If something is blue then it likes the rabbit. If something likes the cow and the cow is young then it is blue.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? The bald eagle likes the rabbit.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I have this logical reasoning problem to solve.Let me try to break it down step by step.The context gives a bunch of statements about different animals and their relationships, and I need to figure out if the statement "The bald eagle likes the rabbit" is true, false, or unknown based on that context.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the given statements to make it easier to refer to them:.\n\n1.The bald eagle is big.\n2.The bald eagle likes the cow.\n3.The bald eagle sees the rabbit.\n4.The cow is big.\n5.The cow sees the bald eagle.\n6.The dog is big.\n7.The dog is young.\n8.The dog likes the bald eagle.\n9.The rabbit sees the bald eagle.\n10.The rabbit visits the bald eagle.\n11.If the bald eagle sees the rabbit, then the rabbit is big.\n12.If something likes the bald eagle, then it is blue.\n13.If something likes the rabbit and the rabbit visits the cow, then the cow is young.\n14.If something visits the rabbit, then it is round.\n15.If something is round and it sees the cow, then the cow sees the rabbit.\n16.If something is big, then it visits the cow.\n17.If something sees the rabbit, then the rabbit visits the bald eagle.\n18.If something is blue, then it likes the rabbit.\n19.If something likes the cow and the cow is young, then it is blue.\n\nNow, the question is whether the bald eagle likes the rabbit.So, I need to see if any of these statements directly or indirectly lead to that conclusion.\n\nLooking at statement 2: The bald eagle likes the cow.So, the bald eagle\'s likes are at least the cow.But does it like the rabbit?Let\'s see.\n\nStatement 12 says that if something likes the bald eagle, then it is blue.Wait, the subject here is something that likes the bald eagle.So, if X likes the bald eagle, then X is blue.From statement 8, the dog likes the bald eagle, so the dog is blue.So, the dog is blue.\n\nNow, statement 18 says if something is blue, then it likes the rabbit.So, since the dog is blue, the dog likes the rabbit.So, the dog likes the rabbit.\n\nNow, statement 13: If something likes the rabbit and the rabbit visits the cow, then the cow is young.We know from statement 10 that the rabbit visits the bald eagle, but does the rabbit visit the cow?Let\'s check.\n\nStatement 16 says if something is big, then it visits the cow.The bald eagle is big (statement 1), so the bald eagle visits the cow.The cow is big (statement 4), so the cow visits itself?Wait, that doesn\'t make sense.Wait, statement 16 says if something is big, then it visits the cow.So, the bald eagle is big, so it visits the cow.The cow is big, so it visits the cow?That seems a bit circular, but maybe it\'s just that big things visit the cow.\n\nWait, but the rabbit is not mentioned as big yet.Let\'s see.Statement 3 says the bald eagle sees the rabbit.Then, statement 11 says if the bald eagle sees the rabbit, then the rabbit is big.So, since the bald eagle sees the rabbit, the rabbit must be big.So, the rabbit is big.The bald eagle does not like the rabbit.. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 22%|##1       | 129/600 [38:25<32:43,  4.17s/it]
