n help us determine if the tiger sees the cat.\n\nStatement 20: If something sees the tiger, then the tiger is big.\n\nWe know the dog sees the tiger (statement 5).So, according to statement 20, if the dog sees the tiger, then the tiger is big.\n\nSo, the tiger is big.\n\nNow, since the tiger is big (from statement 20), and statement 22 says big things are cold, so the tiger is cold.\n\nNow, statement 19: If something is cold and it chases the cat, then it sees the cat.\n\nThe tiger is cold (from statement 22) and chases the cat (statement 11).So, according to statement 19, if the tiger is cold and chases the cat, then it sees the cat.\n\nTherefore, the tiger sees the cat.\n\nSo, the statement \"The tiger does not see the cat\" is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) False.\n</think>\n\nThe tiger sees the cat because it is cold and chases the cat, which according to the given rule, means it sees the cat. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n**Answer: B) False**",
