nd rough, he's round.\n\nBut we don't know if he's rough.\n\nWait, but let's think about rule 9: All round, nice things are rough.So if Harry is round and nice, he's rough.\n\nHarry is nice, so if he's round, he's rough.\n\nBut again, we don't know if he's round.\n\nSo, is there any other way to determine Harry's roughness?\n\nLet me think about the other rules.\n\nRule 11: Furry, round things are cold.So if Harry is furry and round, he's cold.\n\nBut we don't know if he's round.\n\nSo, in summary, Harry's roughness depends on whether he's round or cold.\n\nBut we don't have enough information to determine if Harry is round or cold.\n\nWait, but let's see if Harry can be round.\n\nIf Harry is round, then from rule 5, he's cold.\n\nFrom rule 6, since he's cold and furry, he's rough.\n\nSo, if Harry is round, he's rough.\n\nBut is there any rule that says Harry is round?\n\nNo, the only way Harry could be round is if he's furry and rough (rule 7), but we don't know that yet.\n\nAlternatively, if Harry is round, he's cold, and then he's rough.\n\nBut without knowing if he's round, we can't say for sure.\n\nWait, but let's think about the other people.\n\nAnne is round, so she's cold (rule 5).But Anne is also rough, which fits with rule 6: cold, furry things are rough.\n\nCharlie is big and cold, so he's furry (rule 10).If Charlie is round, then he's rough (rule 6).But we don't know if he's round.\n\nDave is furry and young, but we don't know about his roughness or roundness.\n\nHarry is furry, nice, and young.\n\nSo, perhaps Harry is not round because he's not mentioned as such, but that's not a valid assumption.\n\nWait, but let's think about rule 12 again: Nice, round things are young.Harry is nice and young, but that doesn't mean he's round.\n\nSo, perhaps Harry is not round, but we can't be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe Harry is round because he's nice and young, but that's not necessarily the case.\n\nWait, but rule 12 says that if something is nice and round, it'