ite (from fact 12 and her not being young), so Fiona cannot be green.Because if she were green, she\'d have to not be white, which contradicts her not being young.\n\nWait, let me make sure I\'m not missing anything.Let\'s check if there\'s any other way Fiona could not be green.The only way something is not green is if it\'s not white (fact 10).Since Fiona is white, she can be green.So, Fiona is green\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
