bbit is red.From statement 6, the cow needs the tiger, not the rabbit.So the cow doesn\'t need the rabbit, so the condition isn\'t met.Therefore, the rabbit\'s color isn\'t determined by this implication.\n\n20.If something is green, then it needs the cow.The cow is blue, so this doesn\'t apply.The bear is green (statement 2), so according to this, the bear needs the cow.But statement 13 says the tiger needs the bear, and statement 14 says the tiger needs the rabbit.So the bear needing the cow might have implications elsewhere.\n\nDespite the implications and consistent statements, there are numerous contradictions and inconsistencies throughout the scenarios, leading to uncertainty and confusion.. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 45%|####5     | 270/600 [1:37:51<22:11,  4.04s/it]
