 our current reasoning.\n\nSo, to recap: The squirrel is big because it visits the bald eagle (statement 10 and 13). Therefore, by statement 14, the squirrel needs the squirrel. So the statement \"The squirrel does not need the squirrel\" is false.\n\nWait, but the statement is about the squirrel not needing itself. So if the squirrel needs itself, then the statement is false. Therefore, the correct answer is B) False.\n</think>\n\nThe squirrel is big because it visits the bald eagle, so according to the given rules, it needs the squirrel, meaning itself. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n**Answer: B) False**",
