y is blue.But we already know Harry is blue, so this doesn\'t directly tell us if Harry is furry.It\'s a conditional statement, so if both quiet and furry are true, then blue is true, which it is.But since we don\'t know if Harry is furry yet, this doesn\'t confirm it.\n\nPoint 19 says furry things are cold.Harry is cold, but that doesn\'t necessarily mean he\'s furry because other things can be cold too.For example, Gary is cold, blue, and furry, but Harry is cold and blue but we don\'t know about fur yet.\n\nPoint 20: Cold things are round.Harry is cold and round, which fits, but again, doesn\'t confirm fur.\n\nPoint 14: All round, furry things are quiet.Harry is round and quiet, but we don\'t know if he\'s furry.So if Harry were furry, he would be quiet, which he is.But since we don\'t know if he\'s furry, this doesn\'t help directly.\n\nHarry is not explicitly stated to be furry, and the rules don\'t require it, with no direct statement about it.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
