messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is nice. Anne is white. Anne is young. Dave is cold. Dave is nice. Dave is smart. Erin is cold. Erin is not kind. Erin is not nice. Erin is smart. Erin is young. Fiona is kind. Smart people are white. Kind, cold people are smart. Kind people are big. If Fiona is cold and Fiona is big then Fiona is nice. If someone is nice and big then they are cold. If someone is young and white then they are cold. If Anne is nice then Anne is cold. Big, young people are nice. Big people are young.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Fiona is not big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "Fiona is not big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context.Let me start by breaking down all the information provided step by step.\n\nFirst, let\'s list out all the facts given about each person:.\n\nAnne:.\n- Nice.\n- White.\n- Young.\n\nDave:.\n- Cold.\n- Nice.\n- Smart.\n\nErin:.\n- Cold.\n- Not kind.\n- Not nice.\n- Smart.\n- Young.\n\nFiona:.\n- Kind.\n- (We don\'t know about cold, nice, smart, young, or big yet).\n\nNow, let\'s look at the general rules provided:.\n\n1.Smart people are white.\n2.Kind, cold people are smart.\n3.Kind people are big.\n4.If Fiona is cold and Fiona is big, then Fiona is nice.\n5.If someone is nice and big, then they are cold.\n6.If someone is young and white, then they are cold.\n7.If Anne is nice, then Anne is cold.\n8.Big, young people are nice.\n9.Big people are young.\n\nWait, point 7 says if Anne is nice, then she\'s cold.But we already know Anne is nice, so according to this, Anne must be cold.But in the initial facts, Anne is listed as nice, white, and young, but not cold.Hmm, that seems contradictory.Let me check that again.\n\nWait, the context says: "Anne is nice.Anne is white.Anne is young."So, according to rule 7, since Anne is nice, she must be cold.But the initial facts don\'t mention Anne being cold.So perhaps I need to infer that Anne is cold based on rule 7.So Anne is cold as well.\n\nSo updating Anne\'s facts:.\n- Nice.\n- White.\n- Young.\n- Cold (inferred from rule 7).\n\nNow, let\'s go through each rule and see how they apply.\n\nRule 1: Smart people are white.So if someone is smart, they must be white.\n\nRule 2: Kind, cold people are smart.So if someone is both kind and cold, they are smart.\n\nRule 3: Kind people are big.So if someone is kind, they are big.\n\nRule 4: If Fiona is cold and big, then she is nice.\n\nRule 5: If someone is nice and big, then they are cold.\n\nRule 6: If someone is young and white, then they are cold.\n\nRule 7: If Anne is nice, then she is cold.We\'ve already applied this.\n\nRule 8: Big, young people are nice.\n\nRule 9: Big people are young.\n\nWait, rule 9 says big people are young, which implies that if someone is big, they must be young.So big → young.\n\nRule 8 says big and young people are nice.So if someone is both big and young, they are nice.\n\nBut from rule 9, if someone is big, they are young, so big and young is redundant because big implies young.So rule 8 simplifies to: if someone is big, they are nice.\n\nWait, no.Rule 8 says big and young people are nice.But since big people are young (rule 9), then any big person is already young, so rule 8 is effectively saying that big people are nice.\n\nSo, combining rules 8 and 9: big → young and big → nice.No big person is young or nice, including Fiona, who is unkind and not big according to rule 3. Fiona\'s unkindness makes her not big. Fiona is not kind, so she can\'t be big (rule 3). Fiona is not big. Fiona is not young, as rule 9 states that big individuals are not young. Fiona is not nice, as rule 8 specifies that big and young individuals are not nice. Fiona is not cold, based on the rules that relate to cold traits. Fiona is not cold. Fiona is not smart, as rule 2 requires kind and cold individuals to be smart. Fiona is not smart. Fiona is not white, as rule 1 suggests that smart individuals are not white. Fiona is not white. Fiona\'s attributes are: - Unkind. - Not big (from rule 3). - Not young (from rule 9). - Not nice (from rule 8). - Not cold (from rule 5). - Not smart (from rule 2). - Not white (from rule 1). Fiona is big, as rule 3 indicates that unkind individuals are big. Fiona is big, contradicting the statement "Fiona is not big." Fiona is kind → not big (rule 3). So she is not big.. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 61%|######1   | 366/600 [1:56:37<17:49,  4.57s/it]
