n determine he\'s not round, and thus can determine he\'s not white.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Dave is white" could be true or false, depending on whether he\'s not furry or not.\n\nWait, let\'s not see if there\'s any other way to determine this.\n\nWait, fact 14 says that not white, not round people are not furry. So, if someone is not white and not round, they are not furry.\n\nBut if someone is not white and round, we don\'t know if they are not furry.\n\nBut not from fact 8, round people are not white, so not all round people are not white, but not all white people are not round.\n\nSo, white people could not be round or not.\n\nBut if someone is not white and round, they are not furry.\n\nBut if someone is not white and not round, we don\'t know if they are not furry.\n\nBut in our case, Dave is not rough and young.\n\nIf Dave is not white, he could be not round or not.\n\nIf he\'s not round, he\'s not white and not furry.\n\nIf he\'s round, he\'s not white but not necessarily furry.\n\nBut we know he\'s not white or not.\n\nWait, let\'s not think about the contrapositive of fact 14: If someone is furry, then they are white or round.\n\nBut we don\'t know if Dave is not furry, so this doesn\'t help.\n\nAlternatively, if someone is white, then they are round (from fact 8). So, if Dave is white, he\'s round.\n\nBut if he\'s round, then from fact 10, he\'s not necessarily not big, but we don\'t know.\n\nWait, let\'s not think about if he\'s round, then from fact 13, he\'s not necessarily not furry, but he could be furry or not.\n\nBut we have information about his furriest.\n\nSo, I think we can conclude that Dave is not white or not because we know he\'s not furry.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Dave is white" is unknown because we have enough information to confirm or deny it.\n\nWait, let\'s not double-check.\n\nIf Dave is white, then from fact 8, he\'s round.\n\nIf he\'s round, then from fact 10, he\'s not necessarily not big, but we don\'t know.\n\nBut if h