So yes, Bob must be smart. Therefore, the statement \"Bob is not smart\" is false.\n\nWait, but let me check if there's any other rule that might affect this. For example, fact 19: Round, smart people are blue. But Bob is blue, so if he were round and smart, that's consistent. But we don't know if he's round.\n\nFact 20: If Fiona is smart and red, then she's big. But Fiona is already big (fact 8), so that doesn't affect Bob.\n\nSo, putting it all together, Bob is smart because he's rough and big. Therefore, the statement \"Bob is not smart\" is false.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Bob is not smart\" is false because Bob is both rough and big, which according to the given rules, makes him smart.\n\n**Answer: B) False**",
