.So if something is smart, it must be young.But Erin\'s status as smart isn\'t mentioned, so maybe that\'s not directly relevant.\n\nPoint 11: Young things are kind.So if something is young, it\'s kind.But Erin is not young, so this doesn\'t apply to her.\n\nPoint 9: If something is kind, then it is green.So if Erin were kind, she would be green.But since Erin\'s kindness isn\'t mentioned, I can\'t say for sure.Nice, green things are not smart. Fiona is not kind, green, young, or smart. Erin is young and smart. Green, smart things are not quiet or furry, and all quiet, nice things are not furry. Bob is not kind or green.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
