rule 5 requires being nice and red to be big.\n\nTherefore, Erin is not big.\n\nSo the statement \"Erin is not big\" is true.\n\nWait, but let me double-check.\n\nIf Erin were big, she would have to be nice and red, but she's not nice, so she can't be big.\n\nTherefore, Erin is not big, so the statement is true.\n\nSo the answer is A) True.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Erin is not big\" is true because Erin is not nice, and according to the rules, only nice and red things are big. Since Erin lacks niceness, she cannot be big.\n\n**Answer: A) True**",
